the partial sums equal the closed form exactly for n = 0 to 10: True
limit of the multiplier as n grows, 1 / reserve ratio: 10.0000
limit in cents: 1000000

B. Balance sheet at each stage: reserves plus loans equal the deposits received at that stage
each stage balances: True
cumulative reserves plus cumulative loans equal total deposits: True
total deposits after stage 10, in cents: 686189

C. Leakage variant: only a share of each loan is redeposited, the rest is held as cash
redeposit share 1.00: total deposits after stage 10, in cents =    686189; limit in cents = 1000000
redeposit share 0.50: total deposits after stage 10, in cents =    181790; limit in cents = 181818
the full-redeposit limit exceeds the half-redeposit limit: True

D. Intermediary: a loss on loans reduces equity; deposits are unchanged
assets (loans, in dollars): 1000; deposits: 900; equity: 100
loss 50 dollars: equity after = 50 dollars, deposits after = 900 dollars, equity nonnegative: True
loss 100 dollars: equity after = 0 dollars, deposits after = 900 dollars, equity nonnegative: True
loss 150 dollars: equity after = -50 dollars, deposits after = 900 dollars, equity nonnegative: False
=== tests/labs/FC1/lab-FC1-L02-1.py
A. Each entry has exactly one value on each axis
entries in the register: 12; well formed: 12
every entry is well formed: True

B. Counts on each axis reconcile to the number of entries
exposure: equities 3, rates 3, credit 2, fx 2, commodities 2; total 12; reconciles: True
form: cash 6, derivative 6; total 12; reconciles: True
venue: exchange 4, otc 8; total 12; reconciles: True

C. The venue axis is separate from the form axis: exchange entries by form
exchange entries: 4; cash 1; derivative 3
exposure classes with at least one exchange entry: 3 (commodities, equities, rates)

D. A malformed entry is rejected by the same check
malformed entry rejected: True
exposure total with the malformed entry added: 14 for 13 entries
the exposure total no longer reconciles to the entry count: True
